 "verdict": "MAGNITUDE IS NOT PREDICTABLE FROM BIOLOGY (every biological arm is net-negative; best +CTCF R2 -0.0097 vs permuted -0.0037, net -0.0060) -- but adding DETECTION POWER as a feature reaches R2 +0.0881 (net +0.0928), so effect magnitude in this benchmark is predictable from a technical variable and not from regulatory biology. The marginal correlation of |EffectSize| with power is only -0.058, so this would have been missed without the arm. SIGN IS PARTLY PREDICTABLE (+CTCF: AUPRC 0.6507 vs base rate 0.194, 3.36x lift, AUROC 0.8584). the edge-finder does NOT rank strength where the sample is large: pooled Spearman +0.0863 (p 0.0135) is carried by small cell types, while in K562 (n=717) it is +0.0488 (p 0.192). n=820 causal pairs, so this is a small-sample result and 19.4% of those elements are repressive, a subclass the binary label erases entirely."
